<title>ECUADOR: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>ECUADOR GOVERNMENT LIST (970207)</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>* 7 Feb 97 - President Abdala Bucaram Bucaram was voted out  *</p>
<p>*		of office on Feb 6 by an extraordinary session  *</p>
<p>*		of Congress. Congress then swore in its leader  *</p>
<p>*		Fabian Alarcon, to replace him as interim	 *</p>
<p>*		president as Bucaram vowed defiantly to serve   *</p>
<p>*		out his term. The military said Vice President  *</p>
<p>*		Rosalia Arteaga had also issued a decree	  *</p>
<p>*		declaring her own right to the presidency.</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>President (Took office 10 Aug 96)............**Abdala BUCARAM</p>
<p>							  (**SEE NOTE ABOVE)</p>
<p>Vice President..Rosalia ARTEAGA</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (10 Aug 96)</p>
<p> Agriculture.......Hugo ENCALADA</p>
<p>Defence.....Victor Manuel BAYAS</p>
<p> Education.......Sandra CORREA**</p>
<p>						   (** Resigned 28 Jan 97)</p>
<p> Energy...........Alfredo ADUM**</p>
<p>						    (** Resigned 6 Feb 97)</p>
